<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC
 "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/PolicyKit/1/policyconfig.dtd">
<policyconfig>

  <!-- Mem Reduct Zamak: the only privileged surface.
       One action, one fixed root-owned helper path, one fixed argument.
       The GUI cannot pass a PID, a path, or a shell command through this
       action: pkexec is invoked with a literal argv, and the helper rejects
       anything but "pagecache".

       Defaults are "no" everywhere on purpose: the shipped policy grants
       nothing. An administrator who wants the one-shot page-cache action to
       be usable without editing this file can allow the action id through a
       polkit rules file (50-local.d style); the helper still enforces its
       own fixed argument and root checks regardless of how it was reached.
       There is deliberately no retain_authorization / require_active
       annotation: every request must be authorized again. -->
  <vendor>Mem Reduct Zamak</vendor>
  <vendor_url>https://github.com/MilchstraBe-Endless10/memreduct-linux-zamak</vendor_url>

  <action id="io.github.milchstrasse_endless10.memreduct.zamak.pagecache">
    <description>Drop the file page cache once (Mem Reduct Zamak)</description>
    <description xml:lang="zh_CN">一次性清理文件页缓存（Mem Reduct Zamak）</description>
    <message>Authentication is required to drop the file page cache.

Dropping the cache discards cached file data. Programs will have to read it
back from disk, which can be slower until the cache refills. There is no
guarantee how much memory this returns, and it is a one-shot diagnostic
action, not an optimisation.</message>
    <message xml:lang="zh_CN">清理文件页缓存需要认证。

清理会丢弃已缓存的文件数据，程序需要重新从磁盘读取，缓存回填前系统可能变慢。
无法保证能释放多少内存。这是一次性诊断操作，不是日常优化手段。</message>
    <icon_name>memreduct-zamak</icon_name>
    <defaults>
      <!-- Issue #13 M0: the previously shipped all-"no" defaults made every
           request impossible, so the product could never perform the one
           kernel write it exists to perform ("pkexec refused" is not a usable
           program). The active local session may authorize this single
           fixed action with an administrator password, every time. No
           *_keep variant: approval is never reused. No allow_any or
           allow_inactive: a remote or background session can never authorize
           it. -->
      <allow_any>no</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>no</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>auth_admin</allow_active>
    </defaults>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path">/usr/libexec/memreduct-zamak-helper</annotate>
  </action>

</policyconfig>
